  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sanchalak/Firm Kai Paan Product Pvt. ... vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 21 November, 2025",
    "facts": "3. Challenging the orders passed by the Courts/authority below, it is submitted by counsel for the appellant that the case was decided in utter violation of principle of natural justice. The Examination-in-Chief of Ravi Kumar Shivhare NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2025:MPHC-GWL:30123 2 MSA-18-2024 was recorded on 22-06-2022. However, as the Adjudicating Officer was busy in Sanchalak/Firm Kai Paan Product Pvt. ... vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 21 November, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/79220337/ 1 election duties, therefore the cross-examination was deferred. Thereafter, the case continued up to 26.12.2023 for examination of the departmental witnesses and on 26-12-2023, the following order sheet was recorded:- \" ... FSO PO . \" 4. On 12-01-2024, the right of the appellant to departmental witness was closed. However, the presence of any of the departmental witness was not recorded in the order dated 12-01-2024, and the case was fixed for final arguments. The case was never fixed for recording of defence evidence of the appellants and ultimately, the final order was passed. 5. It is submitted that since no opportunity to cross-examine the departmental witness was extended to the appellant, therefore, evidence of the departmental witness which was not tested by any of the accused, by cross- examining him, cannot be looked into, and further, the valuable right of the appellant to lead defense witness was also not extended.",
    "arguments": "6. Per contra, the appeal is vehemently opposed by the counsel for the State.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "6. Per contra, the appeal is vehemently opposed by the counsel for the State.",
